                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9430640d-38f1-4888-9c56-b6b10db3ab6c",
                        "entry_id": "ae042908-6e57-3235-8ede-9d90c4da2c5d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "métros"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                        "entry_id": "ae042908-6e57-3235-8ede-9d90c4da2c5d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of metro, used for a system in a French-speaking city."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65ac2fd4-ddb0-447b-8f13-bfebeffc8963",
                                "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                                "text": "“Where are we going, Jean-Michel?” He answered jokingly, “To the métro. It’s often much better to take the métro than it is to drive, but we need to hurry. After 7:00 p.m. there are fewer métros that come through the Pont Marie station.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d72e214c-a91f-4ad3-9ca1-529a39dcf8b3",
                                "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                                "text": "On a crisp fall day, traveling by your lonesome during rush hour, the métro is surely your best option. Inflexibly refusing to take the métro because of social cachet or personal inconvenience is just bad policy, when you will have to spend ten times as much at triple the time to get to a specific destination in a taxi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5d115b4-b710-4c48-a90e-0a2ad85b2c82",
                                "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                                "text": "On Day Five, take the métro to Opéra to visit the stunning Opéra Garnier with its mural by Marc Chagall."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db6a2c5a-2a10-4ac2-b54d-7a4c0398caa0",
                                "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                                "text": "And so we can conclude from all this that when Maigret does take the métro, it’s always for a practical purpose, never for the pleasure of the voyage, a pleasure he can find in slumping in the seat of a taxi, or in smoking his pipe on the platform of a bus, while regarding the spectacle of the teeming streets of “his” city[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56389e78-ea2c-4b39-be26-ee833fdd3c1c",
                                "sense_id": "4a63b8a4-788f-3582-8eba-d5257936345e",
                                "text": "Vary your strolling by taking the métro each day to a new neighborhood, even inauspiciously bourgeois ones like the 15th or the 16th arrondissements, and begin your wandering."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
